  "production_ready": false,
  "implementation": [
    "Application-owned immutable bounded catalogue, compiled into the desktop; exact backend model/firmware identity, independent pins/publisher keys and signed-release BLAKE2b digest. No runtime trust import from files, environment or adjacent manifests.",
    "At most one fresh-install offer per exact target; invalid or ambiguous catalogues select nothing. Shipping catalogue intentionally empty because complete RF/reboot/hardware/independent release gates remain open.",
    "Ordinary first-install UI invokes pinned HTTPS download then signed-package and catalogue-digest binding before fresh identity/plan preparation. Exact-plan approval still precedes credential persistence and upload.",
    "Retained non-offered entries support saved-attempt lookup across publisher changes; the existing token, exact plan, identity and package names are reused. The saved journal must stay unchanged while downloading and loading credentials.",
    "Unreadable, invalid, pending or credential-saved local records refuse another fresh identity through the normal UI. Wrong model, firmware or release, changed control session or changed hardware identity refuse preparation.",
    "Development first selection remains a separate compiled development fallback only when the catalogue is empty, with an explicit unqualified banner. It is not production distribution."
  ],
